course: dictionary
lesson: 2276
title: Creep and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. In the sentence «if it makes me grow smaller, I can creep under the door», creep means moving slowly and quietly so no one notices you.
explain: «Cats hunt by waiting, creeping and pouncing» shows creep as moving slowly and quietly towards something before jumping on it. The word pouncing comes next, so the clues help you see what the cat does after creeping.
explain: Creep can also be a noun. A creep is an unpleasant person, and someone who gives you the creeps makes you feel uneasy or afraid. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Creep can be a verb or a noun: creep, creeps, crept, creeping; a creep is a person.
fact: «Creep» means to move slowly and quietly so no one notices you.
fact: «Creep» can also mean to move slowly along the ground, like ivy growing up a wall.
fact: «Creep in» means something slowly appears, like a mistake.
fact: «The creeps» means a feeling of fear or disgust, as in «give someone the creeps».
exercise: «The children crept down the dark stairs.» What does creep mean here? | To fall asleep | *To move slowly and quietly so no one notices | To sing softly | To run fast and loudly
exercise: Ivy began to creep up the old garden wall. What does creep suggest? | To jump high | To break | *To move slowly along, like a plant growing | To make a loud noise
exercise: Find the word in «Cats hunt by waiting, creeping and pouncing» that tells you what the cat does after creeping. | cats | hunt | *pouncing | waiting
test: Tom felt a cold shiver. Something about the stranger gave him the creeps. What does the creeps mean? | *A feeling of fear or disgust | A happy feeling of joy | A sudden sleepy yawn
test: «A mistake crept into the story.» Which meaning fits creep here? | *It slowly appeared without anyone noticing | It was a loud sound | It ran out of the room
exam: In «Creep under the door», which word could replace creep? | Shout | *Sneak | Jump | Dance
